// Crusaders Mainframe — the scanner's baud, found rather than assumed (HW-5).
//
// The GM65-class scanner's configured rate is unrecorded, and the Mega never
// writes to the scanner (TX16 may not be wired), so it cannot set one. With
// `!CFG,SBAUD` 0 the Mega starts at 9600 and, ONLY WHILE IDLE (no overlay, no
// press waiting on the bridge), moves to the next rate in the order 9600 ->
// 115200 -> 57600 -> 38400 -> 19200 -> 9600 after three consecutive garbage
// bursts; it LOCKS at the first rate that yields a clean scan, until reboot or
// a `!CFG,SBAUD`. A non-zero SBAUD is that rate only.
// docs/specs/device-serial-protocol.md v3, "Hardware facts".
//
// Pure: the caller owns the port and re-bauds it when rate() changes.
// No Arduino headers, no heap. C++11 as well as C++17.

